      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <p>Illustrative proposals throughout the scenarios, notes and deep dives below: timings and caps are test inputs, not observed results or verified capabilities of either supplier. Model contribution as AOV × (margin − discount), with unchanged product cost; discount loss is AOV × discount. These figures exclude additional shipping, payment, messaging and return costs. Before every queued action, check current purchase, refund, stock and suppression state and permission for that channel and marketing purpose. Assign one queue owner, pause overlapping flows, and deduplicate replayed events by cart, customer and action; test those checks before enabling any channel.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 1 — B2B cart below MOQ threshold. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 1 favors SMS urgency; watch for duplicate SMS and email within 20 minutes. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 2 — logged-in repeat buyer with saved address. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 2 favors push nudge; watch for welcome discount stacking with cart code. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 3 — international shipping quote sticker shock. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 3 favors no-discount assist; watch for discount on email one before trust proof. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 4 — subscription toggle left on at checkout. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 4 favors email proof; watch for SMS after 9pm local without quiet hours. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 5 — first-time mobile shopper on Instagram traffic. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 1 favors SMS urgency; watch for no suppression after partial refund. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 6 — size matrix with two variants OOS. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 2 favors push nudge; watch for attribution credit on would-have-returned orders. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs ActiveCampaign: scenario 7 — gift message field abandoned mid-flow. At $474 AOV and 56% margin, full-price recovery contributes $265.44 vs $175.38 after a 19% code (Δ $90.06). Ladder touch 3 favors no-discount assist; watch for recovery for fully OOS cart. Email 1 ~93m, email 2 ~29h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
